WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.670
Dustin Diamond - the actor best known for
portraying Samuel "Screech" Powers, the resident

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.750
geek of his friend group, on Saved by the
Bell - has died.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.940
Roger Paul, Diamond's representative, confirmed
the tragic news to The Hollywood Reporter

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.620
on Monday, February 1st, 2021.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:19.510
TMZ also reports that a representative for
Diamond, likely Paul but unnamed in the outlet's

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:23.710
coverage, verified that Diamond died on Monday
morning, with his girlfriend at his side.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.850
He was 44 years old.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.670
In January 2021, it was announced via a statement
posted to Diamond's official Facebook page

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:33.610
that the actor had been diagnosed with lung
cancer.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:39.239
An update posted on January 22nd, 2021 confirmed
that Diamond's diagnosis was "stage 4 small

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:43.370
cell carcinoma," and that he was "being treated
and fighting this."

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:47.580
As of mid-January, Diamond was undergoing
chemotherapy, and his representative noted

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.399
at the time that after a week of treatments,
the people around Diamond hoped to "have a

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:55.120
much better understanding of the severity
of his condition and what treatments he will

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.800
need so that he's comfortable."

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.140
Paul issued a press release, shared with Looper,
during the afternoon of February 1st.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.170
In it, he confirmed that Diamond "did not
suffer" in the time leading up to his death.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.170
Paul wrote,

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:10.510
"He was diagnosed with this brutal, relentless
form of malignant cancer only three weeks

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:11.510
ago.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.560
In that time, it managed to spread rapidly
throughout his system; the only mercy it exhibited

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.969
was its sharp and swift execution.

00:01:17.969 --> 00:01:19.560
Dustin did not suffer.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.780
He did not have to lie submerged in pain.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.210
For that, we are grateful.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.840
Dustin Diamond was a character in and of himself:
an unpredictable spitfire who always left

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.139
us shocked, but never left us bored.

00:01:30.139 --> 00:01:34.530
We are thankful he trusted us enough to share
his genuine, authentic self with our team.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.389
We wish you knew him in the way that we did.

00:01:36.389 --> 00:01:40.810
We please ask that you give room for privacy
to our team and Mr. Diamond's family during

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:45.170
this tragic time, as we grieve and remember
the memories spent together.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.429
This loss is as much stinging as it is sudden."

00:01:47.429 --> 00:01:51.899
Though Diamond began his acting career a few
years before Saved by the Bell, with credits

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:56.539
in projects like American Playhouse and Purple
People Eater, his sitcom character Screech

00:01:56.539 --> 00:02:00.340
was the one that made him a household name
and an icon of pop culture from the late '80s

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.099
through to the new millennium.

00:02:02.099 --> 00:02:06.069
Diamond first brought Screech to life in the
1988 Disney Channel series Good Morning, Miss

00:02:06.069 --> 00:02:09.899
Bliss, which centered around a teacher named
Carrie Bliss and the eighth-grade students

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:11.291
she taught at a junior high in Indiana.

00:02:11.291 --> 00:02:16.420
The show, later known as Saved by the Bell:
The Junior High Years, also starred two other

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:21.879
Saved by the Bell mainstays, Mark-Paul Gosselaar's
Zack Morris and Lark Voorhies' Lisa Turtle.

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:26.569
In 1989, Powers, Morris, and Turtle began
appearing as series regulars on Saved by the

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:31.629
Bell, alongside the other core characters:
Tiffani Thiessen's Kelly Kapowski, Mario Lopez's

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:34.739
A.C. Slater, and Elizabeth Berkley's Jessie
Spano.

00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:38.750
The NBC series, about a group of students
navigating the high school hierarchy and occasionally

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:43.599
confronting some more serious troubles, ran
until 1993, but two spin-offs followed not

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:48.909
long after: Saved by the Bell: The College
Years and Saved by the Bell: The New Class.

00:02:48.909 --> 00:02:52.920
Diamond starred in both - as well as the two
Saved by the Bell movies that aired in 1992

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.859
and 1994, respectively, Saved by the Bell
Hawaiian Style and Saved by the Bell Wedding

00:02:57.859 --> 00:02:59.390
in Las Vegas.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.879
The years that marked Diamond's post-Saved
by the Bell career were filled with ups and

00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:07.329
downs - underscored with the release of the
controversial tell-all book Behind the Bell,

00:03:07.329 --> 00:03:11.719
his involvement in a Saved by the Bell-themed
adult film, his various legal troubles, and

00:03:11.719 --> 00:03:15.720
his appearances on shows like Celebrity Fit
Club and Celebrity Big Brother.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.530
In November 2020, NBCUniversal's streaming
service Peacock rolled out the Saved by the

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.049
Bell reboot series - of which Diamond was
not a part.

00:03:24.049 --> 00:03:27.590
Diamond was disappointed to have not been
included in the revival, especially considering

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:31.709
his fellow cast mates were folded into the
fresh show in one way or another, but showrunner

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:35.499
Tracey Wigfield said that there would be a
possibility for the actor to be included in

00:03:35.499 --> 00:03:37.750
a second season, should he be interested.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:42.300
Sadly, that's now no longer a possibility,
and Diamond's final performance as Screech

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.700
will now forever remain in the "Breaking Belding"
digital short.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.280
Our thoughts are with Diamond's loved ones
during this time of grief.

